    "ID Explanation (for the ones that aren't immediately evident from the song or artist name)": "2047 marks the year that Hong Kong's status as a special administrative region of China (SAR), which grants HK its own economic system separate from mainland China, will officially expire.\n\nThe song itself is about the potential ramifications of China taking full power of Hong Kong once again. The song's narrator asks, \"Is the rise of an Eastern sun gonna be good for everyone?\"\n\nSome believe that China already unofficially took back Hong Kong in 2019-2020 when protests occurred there for a wide variety of reasons and resulted in a much bleaker political atmosphere in its aftermath. One could argue that China is becoming increasingly authoritarian"
